# kw-options-ox: Is ox, a word that only starts with o, still an options line (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: 5
# pc: ODE0019
# ruling: XPPAUT prints Loading new options file:<none.opt> for it, so any word that starts with o (except on) is an options line. Only the message shows it, and run.sh does not check that, so the value is the same whether the line is read or ignored.
x'=0
x(0)=3
par a=5
aux v=a
ox none.opt
@ total=0,dt=1
